e conversion.\\n   - Handle the case where `x` is 0.\\n   - Handle negative values of `x` by converting `abs(x)` and prepending \'-\'.\\n   - Validate `base` to be between 2 and 9.\\n\\n4. **Edge Cases**\\n   - `x` is 0: Return \'0\'.\\n   - `x` is negative: Convert `abs(x)` and prepend \'-\'.\\n   - Invalid `base`: Raise `ValueError`.\\n\\n5. **Complexity**\\n   - Time: O(log_b(x)), where b is the base.\\n   - Space: O(log_b(x)) for storing the result.\\n\\n### Example Implementations\\n```python\\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\\n    if not 2 <= base <= 9:\\n        raise ValueError(\\"Base must be between 2 and 9.\\")\\n    \\n    if x == 0:\\n        return \'0\'\\n    \\n    result = \'\'\\n    is_negative = x < 0\\n    x = abs(x)\\n    \\n    while x > 0:\\n        result += str(x % base)\\n        x //= base\\n    \\n    if is_negative:\\n        result = \'-\' + result\\n    \\n    return result[::-1]\\n```\\n\\nThis checklist ensures all aspects of the function are covered, from validation to edge cases and the core conversion logic."}'}]
